1
00:00:00,283 --> 00:00:03,273
A library can move every book and still lose its

2
00:00:03,273 --> 00:00:03,946
catalog.

3
00:00:04,265 --> 00:00:07,206
A CRM migration must preserve usable meaning:

4
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:14,368
organizations, people, relationships, ownership, history, access, and the commercial measures

5
00:00:14,368 --> 00:00:15,750
employees rely on.

6
00:00:16,807 --> 00:00:20,905
A legacy Contract Value field is not automatically equivalent to

7
00:00:20,905 --> 00:00:22,055
Salesforce Amount.

8
00:00:22,361 --> 00:00:27,506
Confirm gross or net values, currencies, stage meanings, ownership rules,

9
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:29,104
and the objects in scope.

10
00:00:29,436 --> 00:00:33,640
Preserve stable legacy identifiers so records can be traced.

11
00:00:34,685 --> 00:00:38,792
Clean data using agreed rules, then trial the migration in

12
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:40,084
a suitable environment.

13
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,616
Validate relationships and expected workflows.

14
00:00:43,958 --> 00:00:46,538
Potential duplicates require investigation;

15
00:00:47,058 --> 00:00:51,267
two campaigns for one advertiser may be entirely legitimate business

16
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:51,921
records.

17
00:00:52,975 --> 00:00:57,331
In the source’s fictional trial, twenty thousand records become nineteen

18
00:00:57,331 --> 00:00:59,073
thousand nine hundred forty.

19
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:03,645
Twenty five were excluded by scope, twenty failed relationships, and

20
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:06,109
fifteen had unresolved errors.

21
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:10,619
Reconciliation explains the sixty-record gap rather than hiding it.

22
00:01:11,658 --> 00:01:16,738
Compare monetary totals at record level, accounting for filters, currencies,

23
00:01:17,075 --> 00:01:18,900
statuses, and mappings.

24
00:01:19,249 --> 00:01:24,459
Also check relationships, ownership, security, history, and workflows.

25
00:01:24,756 --> 00:01:29,053
Record what changed or was excluded against acceptance criteria agreed

26
00:01:29,053 --> 00:01:31,242
with business and technical owners.

27
00:01:32,298 --> 00:01:37,095
Plan cutover, communications, training, recovery, and monitoring.

28
00:01:37,414 --> 00:01:39,956
The posting says the analyst supports migration;

29
00:01:40,455 --> 00:01:43,149
it does not reveal the legacy system or require this

30
00:01:43,149 --> 00:01:46,231
employee to lead the entire technical project alone.

31
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:48,809
Authorized owners decide readiness.
